==Battleground==
*1 [[Master A.]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*3 [[Dagshund]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*20 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*20 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 21.33 seconds<sup>640f</sup>, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*20 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 22.67 seconds<sup>680f</sup>, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*20 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 24 seconds<sup>720f</sup>, delay 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The strategy for this stage is very simple. Using [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] cats and [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attack]] cats is the way to go here. Use the Dagshunds as a stepping stone to kill the Master A. in the back. After the Master A. dies, you can use ranged attackers to kill off the Dagshunds and the stage should be done. You should avoid killing the Dagshunds before Master A. dies. Syncing up the Dagshunds with the cat cannon is very useful to significantly reduce the pushing power of the enemies.

